# diag-to-tasks.env — environment for the self-fix queue builder
# (integrations/diag-to-tasks.mjs). Copy to the operator's private env path on the box
# and substitute the __PLACEHOLDER__ values. Ships with placeholders ONLY — no real
# hostnames/paths in the repo. There are NO chain keys here: this code reads the same
# read-only probes alpha-e2e does and WRITES only the queue file pair. It signs nothing.

# --- where the queue lives --------------------------------------------------
# The merged work-item queue (stable-id tasks + counts + green streaks). A sibling
# self-fix-queue.md is written next to it automatically for the annal/brief pipeline.
# Put it in the writable DATA_DIR the unit grants (ReadWritePaths), NOT in the repo.
# Point DATA_DIR at the box's brain/shared dir so the queue rides along with the other
# annal/brief shared artifacts. (Falls back to a repo-relative dir only for bare ad-hoc runs.)
DIAG_TASKS_PATH=__DATA_DIR__/self-fix-queue.json

# Consecutive green diagnostics runs before a task is considered recovered and dropped
# from the queue. Default 3 (≈45 min of green at the 15-min cadence). Raise to make
# recovery stickier; lower to clear the queue faster.
# DIAG_RECOVER_AFTER=3

# --- read-side probe config (same vars alpha-e2e.mjs reads) -----------------
# When run under systemd the unit re-runs the e2e probes inline (no pipe), so it needs
# the same surface URLs alpha-e2e uses. Point these at the live testnet / public faces.
# (Read-only; soft-fails per check if a surface is down — that's the whole point.)
# MELEK_RPC_URL=__RPC_URL__
# ALPHA_BASE=__ALPHA_BASE__
# POOL_BASE=__POOL_BASE__
